Subject: Arrays have a storage kind byte, and every legacy access of their elements goes through it (QJS_PACKED_ARRAYS, off by default)

What this does
  - `JSObject` gains `arr_kind` (in padding; the object does not grow): 0 generic (a JSValue array,
    today's), 1 int32, 2 float64. With `QJS_PACKED_ARRAYS` 0 (the default) nothing else changes: the
    member keeps its name, `JS_ARR_VALS(p)` is `p->u.array.u.values`, `js_array_ensure_generic()` is 0.
  - With the flag on, `u.array.u.values` is renamed `values_raw` (a void *), so the compiler finds every
    use. The 114 uses in quickjs.c and the 4 in quickjs-regvm-step.inc are rewritten to `JS_ARR_VALS(p)`,
    which asserts the array is generic, after one of:
      - `js_array_ensure_generic(ctx, p)` (converts in place with `js_array_unpack`) at the entry of the
        mutators that have an error path: convert_fast_array_to_array, delete_property, set_array_length
        (shrinking), expand_fast_array, add_fast_array_element, js_array_store_hole_gap,
        JS_SetPropertyValue (store to an in-range index), JS_DefineProperty (a value on an index),
        js_append_enumerate (destination), regvm_array_from_const (the template);
      - a kind-aware read: js_get_fast_array_element, JS_DumpObject, the finalizer (a packed array has no
        references to release), the mark function (nothing to mark), JS_ComputeMemoryUsage;
      - a refusal, where there is no error path or the caller wants a JSValue pointer: js_get_fast_array,
        qjs_aot_dense, js_concat_direct_append/spread, the push fast path, regvm_put_elem_fast, the
        in-bounds element reads of the stack interpreter and the register interpreter, the array
        iterator, build_arg_list, JS_CopySubArray, the AOT profile of elements: their guards gain
        `JS_ARR_GENERIC(p)` and the slower path, which is kind-aware or unpacks, serves a packed array.
  - A packed array has no holes, lazy markers or references, and is always JS_CLASS_ARRAY.
  - Nothing builds a packed array in this patch except a test hook: `QJS_PACKED_TEST=1` packs every
    small array that is built or stored into (1 in 1024 of the large ones), `QJS_PACKED_TEST=2` also
    prints the pack/unpack counts at exit, so a whole test corpus runs through the packed paths and the
    conversions back.
  - The layout export (`JSAotGenLayout`) carries `packed_arrays` and `off_object_arr_kind`; the generator
    makes every inline test of a holey array (`QJS_AOT_ARR_ODD`) also refuse a non-zero kind.

Why we need it
  Packed element kinds (4 or 8 bytes an element instead of 16, no tag test on a read of a number array)
  are a separate change that the whole engine must be ready for. Renaming the member makes the compiler
  list every place that assumed a JSValue array, so none is missed; the unpack at the mutators keeps
  the invariant that only code written for packed arrays ever sees one.

Pointer hazard
  `u.array.u.values` used to move only when an array grew; with the flag on it also moves when a packed
  array is unpacked. No site holds the pointer across a call that can run JS or unpack: the sites that
  keep `values` in a local (js_array_toSpliced/toSorted/toReversed/slice/with, js_regexp_result_prealloc,
  build_arg_list) read it from an array they just allocated (always generic) and run no JS between the
  fetch and the last use; callbacks (forEach, map, sort, indexOf with a valueOf) go through
  JS_GetPropertyInt64, which fetches the storage again for every element. js_get_fast_array, which hands
  a `JSValue *` to its callers, returns false for a packed array rather than unpacking.
  The kit case packed1.js unpacks arrays from inside forEach/map/sort/reduce/indexOf/join callbacks over
  the same array under asan with QJS_PACKED_TEST=1.

Sites without an error path: the finalizer, the mark function, JS_ComputeMemoryUsage,
  JS_DumpObject (kind-aware, no unpack), js_get_fast_array / qjs_aot_dense / the concat appends / the
  push fast path / regvm_put_elem_fast / the iterators (refuse a packed array, the generic path serves
  it). Every js_array_unpack call has an error path.
